# Safety Restrictions

## File System Safety
- Never run `rm -rf` on `~/` (home directory)
- Exercise extreme caution with recursive delete operations

## System Access
- Under no circumstances should you run `sudo`
- All commands SHALL be done in userspace
- Never escalate privileges

## Command Line Safety
- Do NOT use `!` in strings meant for the command line / bash
- Escape special characters appropriately when constructing shell commands
